<title>UK: Copper concentrate bulker aground off Nova Scotia.</title>
<headline>Copper concentrate bulker aground off Nova Scotia.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Panama-flagged bulker Ypapadi ran aground off Nova Scotia on December 7 carrying 2,500 tonnes of copper concentrate, Lloyds Shipping Intelligence Service said on Friday.</p>
<p>The 30,330 dwt vessel grounded on sand around latitude 48 51n, longtitude 64 25.2w and was understood to have not sustained any damage.</p>
<p>Some cargo has been offloaded and an unsuccessful attempt to refloat it by two tugs was made on December 12. A further refloating attempt would be made on December 13.</p>
</text>
